WEBVTT

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.090
This is a power curve.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.300
Though it was good enough, I still revised it.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.460
And this is a torque curve.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:49.570
You understand, right? It peaks at 6000rpm and then drops.

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:53.360
That's the reason why you feel a loss of speed or loss of power.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.180
Is it due to the lack of fuel?

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.350
It's the opposite. The fuel is rich, in other words, too thick.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.550
You need to lower the point where maximum torque is generated.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.760
You only care about the maximum power.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.440
Reduce starting from where the rpm generates maximum torque.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:15.090
That's a point. If you continue increasing, the torque will fall easily.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.450
Though, most of the ready-made
CPUs in the market have this setting.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.160
How come? It's not good, right?

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.540
That's because it's safer.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:31.410
If it's too thick the engine won't blow, but if
it's too thin, especially for a turbo car, it would.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.630
As of now, the maximum torque occurs around 6000rpm.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.680
The torque value is not bad and the rpm range is good.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:46.190
From here on, reduce the point of the max
power to 8500rpm, until a gentle curve is shown.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:52.190
However, just like Kitami-san said, the
danger of a sudden engine blow is there.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.340
First of all, we'll spend the next two weeks changing the settings.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:02.660
Note down in detail any occurrences, no matter how trivial.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.840
If possible, it'd be good if there's two persons in the car.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.100
Even under the same circumstances,
what they experience can be different.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.370
How about this, if you have time, go sit next to him.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.120
Give it a shot, Missy...

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.900
Let me confirm this once more, Akio.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.640
If you're seriously aiming higher, you must never forget this.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.140
You're at the risk of a blowout at all times.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:33.900
Has it changed?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.750
It has changed and by a lot.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.900
Just by changing the settings once, the car can change so much...

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.800
<i>I can really go. Amazing.</i>

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.910
<i>Is this what it means to have insufficient torque?</i>

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.990
<i>But, somehow... perhaps it's just my imagination.</i>

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:57.130
<i>I feel as if an ominous presentiment is certainly increasing.</i>

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.640
<i>Flat Racing's R33...</i>

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:10.480
<i>He stopped around Tatsumi Parking.</i>

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:25.360
<i>It's fast. It's totally different than before.</i>

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:37.040
<i>I definitely won't let you escape. I've got you within range now.</i>

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:46.360
<i>Reunion</i>

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.470
<i>There's no leak from the boost.</i>

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.100
<i>And no sense of speed loss during acceleration time.</i>

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.520
<i>It's perfect, no doubt. Until now, it's the best condition so far.</i>

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:03.030
<i>But can I go beyond that? That R33...</i>

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.710
<i>This sense of stability...</i>

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.530
<i>Where can you find another car which can run as straight as this?</i>

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:14.200
<i>People who think that top speed is just about
flooring the accelerator on a straight road,</i>

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.630
<i>can never understand this field of racing.</i>

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.000
<i>Their car will never run straight.</i>

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.510
<i>There's not a single car running straight here in this territory.</i>

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:31.940
<i>To churn out 300km/h on the streets means that
inevitably, you'll keep turning corners at around 250km/h.</i>

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.600
<i>I can't catch up. He'll pull away if I
let my guard down even for a second.</i>

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:44.150
<i>Good job making it this far, Flat Racing, Kuroki Takayuki.</i>

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.820
<i>How is it, Yasu-san? It's pretty good, right?</i>

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.980
<i>I've re-modified everything, including the turbine and engine.</i>

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:54.490
<i>I'm now putting pressure on that BlackBird.</i>

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:03.050
<i>Keirin Island heading towards North Haneda Tunnel.
The problem starts after there.</i>

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.270
<i>Air temperature's up. All electric fans on.</i>

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.490
<i>Oil temperature synchronized and rising.</i>

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:33.990
<i>From high revs and high load to a sudden halt,
from moving wind to zero, engine heating up...</i>

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:40.650
<i>This is tough... Usually I enter a cooling
store from the South Haneda Tunnel.</i>

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:44.000
<i>But this time, I intentionally accelerated until the very last second.</i>

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.480
<i>You seem fine over there.</i>

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:48.500
<i>That's great, even though you're just a coupe.</i>

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.500
<i>It's no good. Overheat.</i>

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.520
<i>Ok, cleared, R!</i>

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.170
<i>Come on, it's Kanagawa's high speed area!</i>

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:05.240
<i>He's pulling away. Shifted from 2nd to 3rd gear.
I can't keep up with that acceleration.</i>

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.240
<i>I completely lose to him in power!</i>

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:20.700
<i>Wangan Kanagawa Line, the only over
320km/h stage in Kanto Area, no, in Japan.</i>

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.810
<i>I can do it. The engine's very agile.</i>

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:27.460
<i>Is the max 320km/h? Or can it go even further?</i>

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.050
<i>It ends here, BlackBird!</i>

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.390
<i>Clutch? Transmission?</i>

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.690
<i>No, this is...</i>

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.870
<i>As expected, it has too much power.</i>

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:43.150
<i>That's why something like that happened suddenly.</i>

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.610
<i>It engages properly, if I slow down this much.</i>

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.160
<i>It's when I shift up from 4th gear.</i>

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:55.440
<i>It can't enter 5th gear due to high rev and high load.</i>

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.370
<i>This is not a problem with the transmission or clutch itself.</i>

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.970
<i>I'm afraid it's the engine mount.</i>

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:05.220
<i>The mount which supports the engine cannot withstand
the high revolutions and unexpectedly got displaced.</i>

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.380
<i>Or perhaps there's a crack.</i>

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:14.260
<i>Tuning is based on marvelous balance. I've always thought so.</i>

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:18.390
<i>But to reach that level, that kind of thing doesn't matter anymore.</i>

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.600
<i>It became a threat when I lowered the mount in order
to reduce the center of gravity as much as possible.</i>

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:26.980
<i>When I loaded the newly assembled engine on the car body,</i>

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.110
<i>I suddenly became worried about the mount.</i>

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:32.490
<i>Whether it could withstand the increased power or not...</i>

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.320
<i>I was in my best condition.</i>

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.050
<i>But I deceived myself.</i>

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.870
<i>Telling myself that I was alright.</i>

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.000
<i>I will never forget, this feeling of defeat.</i>

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:03.300
The thoughts that you and the Missy
recorded, are both pretty interesting.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:08.650
The Missy is feeling even more than
you feel from the center of yourself.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.570
Do you understand what I'm trying to tell you?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.900
It was the right choice, to get her to sit next to you.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:22.910
Ok, let's go with this today. It's quite an interesting specification.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.910
Well, you two go have fun.

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.630
You're getting married, right?

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.300
I heard about it.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.300
He's an editor for a major publishing company, right?

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.510
Congratulations.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.390
No, it's not confirmed yet.

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:39.720
Why are you hesitating now?

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.640
That guy?

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.710
Just get over him.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.640
After all, that guy is living in a different world.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:00.570
<i>As expected, there's a crack in the mount.
It's downright not strong enough.</i>

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:08.330
<i>With just one setting, the driving style changed.</i>

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:18.010
<i>It's as if the Z keeps on showing me new faces.</i>

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.240
How is it? This is pretty much the feeling
that you are aiming for, right, Akio-kun?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.550
It's the best one so far. Even a slight
tap of the accelerator pushes it forward.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:34.030
Do you also think it's good, Reina?

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.240
At first I thought it was great.
No, Akio-kun if you like it then...

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:42.200
Don't worry about it, just tell me.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.450
I see...

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:48.000
It's true that the way your line curved is good,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.210
and the engine also functioned well, even in the higher levels,

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.960
but I feel that the speed is not as I had imagined.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.560
I'm sorry. It's just that, I felt that way.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.960
Ok, why don't you drive then, Reina?

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:01.450
Me?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.560
I'm not the reliable now.

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:09.340
<i>Just get over him already.</i>

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:12.590
<i>After all, that guy is living in a different world.</i>

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.040
<i>A crack in the mount? How naive.</i>

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:29.450
<i>Your welding is too beautiful. Is a nice finishing so important?</i>

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:32.250
<i>You have to do it with a bang.</i>

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:36.250
Really, I've always been doing such a naive work.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:43.260
<i>Are you doing fine somewhere out there, Yasu-san?</i>

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:48.310
<i>I'm now living a full life, for the first time since I was born.</i>

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.680
Good evening.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.240
Mika?

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.170
It's been a while...

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:07.890
Once more, I want to try gathering material
regarding you, the person known as Kuroki Takayuki.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.900
Didn't you quit?

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:13.750
Just now, by chance I met the Chief Editor of Tuning Monthly,

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.250
and he asked me to write an article for it once again.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:21.960
Recently, I keep recalling what you told me the first time we met.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.960
What did I say to you?

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:29.930
You said that your actions on Wangan
have no solid reasoning behind it,

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.010
just that there's a strong attraction to it.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:36.800
I see... so I said that...

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:40.740
I left without knowing the true meaning behind those words.

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:46.110
I want to confirm it with my own eyes once more,
and make a definite conclusion to all of this.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.530
It's the car's instability.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:54.370
There's a sense of speed loss at around
4000 when the accelerator is released.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.050
But if you accelerate then it stabilizes again.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.370
It emerges before I can feel it.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:03.220
What's wrong?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.230
Having fun?

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:06.890
It's fun.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:10.860
I never knew that settings would be so in-depth.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.890
Day after day, the way of driving the car is different.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.190
What is it?

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.650
Just as I thought, your hand is not stiff at all.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.200
Show me your other hand too.

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:27.150
It's unbelievably soft.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:31.150
You can't grip the transmission and steering wheel forcefully.

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:32.370
Try touching my hands.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.490
They're pretty rough, right?

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.060
It's different between men and women.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.130
This leads to a difference in driving style too...

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.940
But you don't use force in any part of your style, Reina.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.380
I clearly understood it today.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.350
You don't fight the overflowing power,
and entrust it to the car's movement,

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.920
and swiftly control the throttle.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.430
Therefore, you trust the car to go where you want it to go.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:01.950
The settings done day after day will be over soon.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:05.730
As much as I can, I want to feel how
it's like to honestly set it like you.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:08.160
I want to choose the best setting.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:13.370
I'm glad you're here Reina, as well as Z.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.710
The Devil Z?

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.420
It means everything to me now.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:24.600
For that, I suspended operations at my shop and completed this R.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:29.870
To race with that Z, it feels like I've
been waiting for it these past 10 years.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.920
Will we meet him tonight? This Z?

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:32.430
Probably.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.640
If you wish to meet it.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.360
It's that sort of car, definitely.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:49.010
It's kinda nostalgic. We used to drive a lot here, C1.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:52.750
Mika, why did you appear before me again?

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.300
You getting coverage is just an excuse, right? I'm no good.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:58.120
I'll only push you away again.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:07.800
That time, and even now, I've known
that your heart always belonged to tuning.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:08.890
Then, why?

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.640
Don't misunderstand.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.850
Really, this time I decided this on my own.

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:17.450
That time I couldn't catch up to you at all.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:20.140
It's not because you pushed me away.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:25.400
I wanted to know everything about you, but that was impossible.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:30.610
No matter how much I think, I realized that
there were some areas where I just can't access.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.290
Mika, I...

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.390
The one in front...

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:38.200
It's Kuroki-san's...

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:44.940
Mika-san?

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:45.890
Reina-chan!

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:50.230
That Z is?

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.900
We finally meet for real.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.870
As long as I wish for it to happen.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.220
You're right...

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.990
What are you gonna do? Will you race him?

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:03.060
No, Kuroki-san doesn't seem to be following.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:13.990
In these two weeks, we tried two biggest setting patterns for the Z.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.410
We'll start with the one Akio chose.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.790
That's good. A torque curve which nicely
cuts through the peak and the drops.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.040
The boost's start is good too.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.380
As expected. The data clearly proves it.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.090
This is the 4th day's data?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:30.950
Yeah.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.050
But I won't be complementing Missy's one though.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.810
The setting Reina chose, can you display it?

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.560
It won't do at all.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.560
At first, I thought it was an interesting setting.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:48.310
A simulated setting and an actual run is different in the end.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.070
Why did you choose this?

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:52.320
I just simply...

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.230
Simply what?

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.830
Because it was fun, I just felt like it that day.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:00.650
It's true that in this run the balance wasn't off,

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:03.840
but it's the first time I've felt so close to the Z.

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:05.760
How should I put it?

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:11.630
I can't really describe it, but on that day
there's no mistaking it, the Z was by my side.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:16.350
Well, this sort of thing can't really be considered reasoning...

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:17.690
No, it does.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.890
It's more than enough.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.440
It's your Z, you be the judge.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.760
Then, please go ahead with this.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.900
The setting that Reina chose.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.010
When did you start photography?

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.050
Around 2 years ago.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.200
I'm just a freelancer, so I can't really do much yet.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:40.930
Does it bother you?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.960
No, not at all.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:45.210
Even though you hated it so much when
I was doing coverage on you last time?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:49.290
Even now, I don't like it. But you need it, right, Mika?

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:50.150
Yeah.

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:51.200
What article are you writing?

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.050
Tell me a bit about it.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:58.720
Flat Racing's representative, Kuroki Takayuki.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.920
Hitting the 200mph mark at Yatabe with a GT-R,

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:07.730
he joined the organization of tuners,
R200 Club, as the  youngest member.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:12.080
Even though the other members shifted
towards course-related activities,

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:14.240
he didn't care and continued on the streets.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.990
Not instructed by anyone, alone,
he devoted himself to nothing but Rs.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:22.890
The R is the only car he seeks.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:26.790
Work increased and even when he was
a tuner that rose to fame in a short while,

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:29.790
he suddenly dismissed all his staff,

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:34.050
shouldered everything on his own and strived for perfection.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:40.050
But now, Kuroki Takayuki has totally canceled all his work.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:45.600
To complete his R perfectly, in order to race with the Z.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.510
Yeah.

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:50.880
Perhaps, Kuroki Takayuki will just fade away like this.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:54.660
Washed away by the flow, a tuner that disappeared.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:19:01.080
However, if that happens and your instinct is to
continue racing, then there's nothing else I can say.

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:05.300
No matter the result, this time I won't run away.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:07.330
I will observe until the very end.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.380
He's fast...!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.180
We were completely ignored by him!

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.720
<i>That day when the colors faded.</i>

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:30.190
<i>Since the race with Flat Racing's R33,
my feelings toward this car are fading as I accelerate.</i>

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:39.700
<i>Even with this 911 that I can't get out of my
mind, which I race with my life on the line.</i>

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.050
I was really surprised that time.

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.600
Me too.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:52.590
The person whom you broke up with, was it him, Kuroki-san?

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.670
Who knows, I wonder...

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:57.620
The Z's settings should be done soon, right?

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.530
Our part is done.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:02.180
The final settings will be done by those guys.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:08.560
The legendary tuner, Kitami Jun and the
CPU devil, Tominaga Kou, amazing right?

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.890
He's really amazing, Akio-kun.

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:13.440
No, I meant you, Reina-chan.

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.240
What do you mean?

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:20.610
It feels good, right? Being recognized and also needed.

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:21.740
Well...

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.620
He went along with the setting that you chose, right?

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:25.990
How did you know?

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.980
Tuners are peculiar people.

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:32.700
Not choosing a road that everyone knows can speed easily,

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:36.000
they purposely pick the road with the most risks.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.490
Not caring about gains or losses,

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:41.590
like their hearts pointing to them,

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:44.260
telling them they have to go no matter what.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:48.030
Since you're the one with the most direct outlook of the Z,

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:50.310
and understand the Z honestly,

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.460
that's why their hearts also point towards you.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:05.990
It's been a while, how are you, Kuroki?

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.040
I've brought you some customers...

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.740
It's been ages since I saw you, Tominaga-san.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:11.830
You're Kitami-san, right?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.600
Nice to meet you, I'm Kuroki.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:15.540
And...

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.540
I'm Shima Tatsuya, thanks for that time.

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:23.050
You think the BlackBird lost?

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.350
No such thing, I'm the one who lost.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:30.300
No matter the reason, it's a fact I hesitated.

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:33.500
That's why I said you were not being yourself.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:36.550
It was only one stage in Wangan.

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:40.120
It was you who selected that course out of all the areas in Shutokou.

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.850
In the end, what do you want to do?

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:44.360
Would you take a ride?

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:47.120
On my 911.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:50.340
Because the race with your R the other day,

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:53.790
my world has completely faded and I couldn't get my mind off it.

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:02.670
<i>Amazing, so this is the 911...</i>

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:12.100
You were fast, even though it's just a few days ago.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.570
So, how was it?

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:16.970
Let me hear your honest opinion.

00:22:16.970 --> 00:22:18.920
It's good, extremely.

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:21.110
I'm still having goosebumps thinking about it.

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:24.810
It's true, I have nothing to say about it.

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:27.110
I see. Thank you very much.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:28.860
Isn't that the opposite?

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:30.070
Opposite?

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.720
Since you can't get your mind off that car,

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:36.120
don't you feel that you want to get closer to it?

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:43.120
See, isn't this great?

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:47.880
I've not faded at all. It can still go on, this car.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:52.500
You handle this thing called a car, as a machine.

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:55.140
I think that's definitely the correct attitude.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:23:00.440
But, there exists a greater attachment to this machine.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.710
Coming this far, thinking things like "this car is bad",

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:07.280
understanding the car's pain and pushing it forward.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:13.200
They have the same scent, the Z and this BlackBird.
